      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is overly defensive and very slow when converting a repository with a large number of refs.\n\nI know that typically `HEAD` points to an unborn ref only when the repository is empty; however, a repository with millions of refs and `HEAD` still pointing to an unborn ref is possible, and it would be a non-corrupted repo, which would then be eligible for conversion.\n\nA simple check that the target SHA1 is `null` would be enough and avoid the full rescanning of all refs.\n\nThe suggested code would still work and pass all tests.\n\n```suggestion\n\t\tif (head !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 head.isSymbolic() \u0026\u0026 head.getTarget().getObjectId() \u003d\u003d null) {\n```",
